{"name":"All Nighter","hex":"#455454","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"all nighter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of all-nighter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all_nighter"}],"entries":[{"title":"All Nighter (film)","blocks":[{"text":"All Nighter is a 2017 American comedy film directed by Gavin Wiesen and written by Seth W. Owen. The film stars J. K. Simmons, Emile Hirsch, and Kristen Schaal. Principal photography began on July 6, 2015, on locations in Los Angeles, California."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/All_Nighter_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Nighter_(film)"},{"title":"The Allnighter (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Allnighter is a 1987 American comedy film directed by Tamar Simon Hoffs and starring Susanna Hoffs, Dedee Pfeiffer, Joan Cusack and Pam Grier. It was released on May 1, 1987."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ad/Allnighterposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Allnighter_(film)"},{"title":"All Nighter (bus service)","blocks":[{"text":"The All Nighter is a night bus service network in the San Francisco Bay Area, California. Portions of the service shadow the rapid transit and commuter rail services of BART and Caltrain, which are the major rail services between San Francisco, the East Bay, the Peninsula, and San Jose. Neither BART nor Caltrain operate owl service due to overnight track maintenance; the All Nighter network helps fill in this service gap. The slogan is, \"Now transit stays up as late as you do!\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Allnighter-511.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Nighter_(bus_service)"},{"title":"Night game","blocks":[{"text":"A night game, also called a nighter, is a sporting event that takes place, completely or partially, after the local sunset. Depending on the sport, this can either be done under low-light conditions or with the use of floodlights. The term \"night game\" is typically used only in reference to sports traditionally held outdoors; although indoor sporting events often take place after local sunset, these events are artificially lighted regardless of the time of day they take place."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_game"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Muni_route_N_Owl_bus%2C_August_2018.JPG/500px-Muni_route_N_Owl_bus%2C_August_2018.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Muni_route_N_Owl_bus%2C_August_2018.JPG/1280px-Muni_route_N_Owl_bus%2C_August_2018.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Muni_route_N_Owl_bus%2C_August_2018.JPG/500px-Muni_route_N_Owl_bus%2C_August_2018.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"N-Judah Owl Muni bus at Market and Fifth (August 2018)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuni_route_N_Owl_bus%2C_August_2018.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Night_game_fenway_park.jpg/500px-Night_game_fenway_park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Night_game_fenway_park.jpg/500px-Night_game_fenway_park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A night game at Fenway Park, a U.S. baseball park in Boston, Massachusetts.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANight_game_fenway_park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip